Yes, it's the Lucia day, 13th of December.  That day is celebrated also
among the Swedish-speaking minority of Finland but is generally known in
the whole country...  It's called celebration of light.  Lucia was an
Italian saint, if I remember correctly.  Her eyes were renowned for
their beauty, and one man was especially enamoured in them.  So she tore
out her eyes and sent them to him; the legend says God let her see again
after that.

Earlier real candles were used commonly by "Lucia maids" (maidens?) but
electric ones are usual today. :> In Finland, the "official" Lucia is
crowned and watched on the steps of the Helsinki Cathedral.  (I know
little about Lucia customs in Sweden.)

